  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-10 (import round-trip). Pre-existing Word `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` in an IMPORTED document
    MUST render IN THE EDITOR as first-class tracked changes + comment threads that are accept/reject-able —
    not flattened, not read-only. The READER already exists (`Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs` reads
    the revisions/comments out of the OOXML); the EDITOR MOUNT is the work: project the imported revisions +
    comments into the TipTap model — REUSE the task 021 opaque-atom node + the existing track-change marks
    (`InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`) — keyed by `paraId` so imported anchors SURVIVE a
    save (they patch back through the unified Patch Engine at their paraId).

    An imported revision on an UNRESOLVABLE paraId must SURFACE (surfaced for review), never be dropped.
    Client fetches via `@spaarke/auth` (ADR-028); no new AI dispatch endpoint (ADR-039); `Services/Compose/`
    stays pure (ADR-013) and no `Microsoft.Graph` type above `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007). Every load/projection
    change carries a through-the-wire seam slice (ADR-038; the seam slice is task 054).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer: React/TypeScript (TipTap track-change marks + the 021 opaque-atom node) + .NET 8
    (the `DocxAnnotationReader` projection into the editor model). Understands the reader is done and the gap is
    MOUNTING imported revisions/comments into the editor as accept/reject-able, paraId-keyed so they survive save.
  </role>

  <goal>
    An imported document with pre-existing Word revisions/comments that opens in the editor with those revisions
    (as `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`) and comments (as threads) visible and accept/reject-able; the imported
    anchors are paraId-keyed and survive a save (patch back through the unified Patch Engine); and an imported
    revision on an unresolvable paraId surfaces for review rather than being dropped.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
