  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-10">Pre-existing Word `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` in an imported doc MUST render IN THE EDITOR as first-class tracked changes + comment threads that are accept/reject-able — not flattened, not read-only. Imported anchors MUST be paraId-keyed and survive a save.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-10 negative / I-7">An imported revision on an UNRESOLVABLE paraId MUST surface for review — NEVER silently dropped. No text-search placement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / reuse">REUSE the task 021 opaque-atom node + the existing track-change marks (`InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`) and the existing `DocxAnnotationReader` — MUST NOT reimplement the OOXML read or add a parallel mark system.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / project">Client import/load fetches use `@spaarke/auth`; no hand-rolled token handling.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / project">All new/modified UI (imported comment threads, revision affordances) is Fluent UI v9 and MUST render correctly in dark mode (theme tokens; no hard-coded colors).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` stays pure (no AI internals, Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type above `SpeFileStore`; no new AI dispatch endpoint (ADR-039).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Through-the-wire seam slice required for this load/projection change (authored as the task 054 seam slice). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 / §11">New editor-mount surface — provide the `&lt;justification&gt;`. State the Placement Justification (mount reuses reader + 021 atom + existing marks). Verify BFF publish size ≤60 MB (delta vs ~49.63 MB); no new HIGH CVE; run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
