    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing revision/comment reader" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs">
        Already reads pre-existing `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` out of the OOXML — project ITS output into the editor model; do not reimplement the read.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Track-change marks + opaque atom (reuse)" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/">
        Reuse `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark` + the task 021 opaque-atom node to mount imported revisions/comments as first-class, accept/reject-able, paraId-keyed.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (frontend + bff-api + docx; xhigh; sonnet). Load the knowledge files + design §4 F4/§5. Read `DocxAnnotationReader.cs`, the 021 opaque-atom node, and the track-change marks. State the Placement Justification. Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Project reader output to editor model">Project the `DocxAnnotationReader` output (imported `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment`) into the TipTap model as `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark` + comment threads, reusing the 021 opaque-atom node for non-renderable imported constructs. Key every imported anchor by paraId.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Mount into the editor, accept/reject-able">Mount the imported revisions + comment threads in `ComposeEditor.tsx` so they are visible and accept/reject-able (they participate in the existing track-change accept/reject flow). Fluent v9, dark-mode-safe.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Survive save + surface unresolvable">Ensure imported anchors are paraId-keyed and survive a save (patch back through the 030 unified Patch Engine at their paraId). An imported revision on an unresolvable paraId surfaces for review (never dropped) — fire the escalation trigger if a drop would be needed.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Tests">Author client component tests (real editor state): imported revisions render as accept/reject-able marks; imported comments render as threads; unresolvable-paraId revision surfaces. If the BFF projection changed, add/update the `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` slice. Include an ADR-021 dark-mode check.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Verify + size/CVE report">`npm run build:prod` the shared lib + `dotnet build`; run tests + Tier-1 NetArchTest. Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`. Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The READER (`DocxAnnotationReader.cs`) reads pre-existing `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` out of the OOXML, but nothing MOUNTS imported revisions/comments into the editor — an imported redlined doc opens without its revisions visible or editable.</existing>
    <extension>Partial reuse: the reader is reused (not reimplemented), the 021 opaque-atom node + the existing track-change marks are reused for the render; the NEW surface is the projection-into-TipTap MOUNT that keys imported anchors by paraId so they survive save. It cannot fold into the reader (server read, no editor model) nor into the marks (which render our own edits, not imported ones from the reader).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the mount, an externally-redlined document (e.g. the CIPO doc, which has track changes) opens WITHOUT its revisions/comments visible or accept/reject-able — the reader's output is stranded. Concrete failing contract: FR-10 / Success Criterion 6 "a doc redlined externally in Word opens with those revisions/comments visible and accept/reject-able" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>An imported revision/comment whose paraId is UNRESOLVABLE in the current projection (Word regenerated or stripped the paraId on an external save) that cannot be surfaced for review without dropping it — STOP and escalate per root §6 rather than silently dropping an imported revision. Silent drop violates FR-10 / I-7.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (imported revisions/comments mounted, accept/reject-able, paraId-keyed)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ (imported-revision projection into track-change marks + opaque atoms)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/importRoundTrip.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ (seam slice if the BFF projection changed)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A doc redlined externally in Word (e.g. the CIPO doc, which has track changes) opens with those revisions (as `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`) and comments (as threads) VISIBLE and accept/reject-able in the editor.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Imported anchors are paraId-keyed and SURVIVE a save — they patch back through the unified Patch Engine at their paraId (reusing the existing `DocxAnnotationReader` + 021 opaque-atom + track-change marks, not a parallel system).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an imported revision on an unresolvable paraId SURFACES for review — it is not silently dropped (and not text-searched into place, I-7).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client fetches use `@spaarke/auth`; `Services/Compose/` injects no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` above `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007); no new AI dispatch endpoint (ADR-039).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Imported comment threads + revision affordances render correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (ADR-021); publish size ≤60 MB (delta vs ~49.63 MB); no new HIGH CVE; client + BFF builds green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Imported revisions render accept/reject-able">
      <steps>Import a doc containing pre-existing `w:ins`/`w:del` (the CIPO doc). Open it in the editor.</steps>
      <expected>The revisions render as `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark` and can be accepted/rejected in the existing track-change flow.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Imported comments render as threads">
      <steps>Import a doc containing pre-existing `w:comment` threads.</steps>
      <expected>The comments render as comment threads anchored at their paraId; they are visible and interactable.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Imported anchors survive a save">
      <steps>Import a redlined doc, make no change, save, reload.</steps>
      <expected>The imported revisions/comments remain at their paraId anchors after the round-trip (paraId-keyed patch-back).</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Unresolvable-paraId revision surfaces">
      <steps>Import a doc whose imported revision references a paraId not present in the current projection.</steps>
      <expected>The revision surfaces for review rather than being dropped; no silent loss.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the imported revisions + comment threads under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Marks, threads, and affordances use theme tokens and are legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    The through-the-wire proof (imported revisions/comments accept/reject-able and survive save) is authored as
    the task 054 seam slice under `tests/integration/seam/Compose/`. Import mount is a separate surface from the
    050/051/052 save path (parallel-safe true). Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR.

    COMPLETED 2026-07-22. Step 0 context load found the R3 base this branch extends already shipped the FULL
    mount (not just the reader): `importedRevisions.ts`/`importedComments.ts` (R3 tasks 050/051) already project
    `ImportedRevision[]`/`ImportedComment[]` onto `InsertionMark`/`DeletionMark`/`CommentAnchorMark`, paraId-primary
    anchored; `ComposeEditor.tsx` already wires both into BOTH mount paths (server-projection + mammoth fallback);
    `ComposeService.LoadAsync` already runs the existing `DocxAnnotationReader` and projects the result onto Load
    (no `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs` change needed — deviation from the POML's suggested step 1, server work
    had already landed); `usePendingRedline.accept`/`.reject` already scan the live document by ledgerRef
    (not gated on hook `pending` state), so the SAME per-change popover already accept/reject-s an imported
    revision's `imported:{id}` ledgerRef unmodified.

    The GAP actually closed: invariant I-7 ("surfaces for review, never silently dropped") was already satisfied
    for COMMENTS (`groupImportedComments` is pure, always seeds the FR-23 panel regardless of anchor resolution)
    but NOT for REVISIONS — `applyImportedRevisions` computed an `unresolved` count that `ComposeEditor.tsx`
    discarded at both call sites, so an unresolvable revision rendered nothing and surfaced nowhere. Fixed:
    `applyImportedRevisions` now returns `unresolvedItems: ImportedRevision[]`; new
    `renderUnresolvedRevisionPlaceholders` (same file) REUSES the task-021 opaque-atom node (`composeInlineAtom`,
    zero new schema) to surface each unresolved revision as a review marker APPENDED at the document end (never
    a guessed in-place position — I-7 bans text-search placement), run as a separate pass after the main
    resolution loop so an earlier placeholder never pollutes a later revision's fuzzy search. Wired into
    `ComposeEditor.tsx` at both mount sites, before the paraId snapshot/op-log reset (same load-time-baseline
    contract every other import-mark helper follows) + folded into the existing `onImportWarnings` banner as a
    privacy-safe count. Dark mode (ADR-021): zero new CSS — reuses the `.compose-atom`/`.compose-atom-inline`
    rules `ComposeEditor.opaqueAtomTheme.test.ts` already proves token-based.

    Escalation trigger did NOT fire — the placeholder mechanism surfaces every unresolved revision without ever
    needing to drop one; no schema change required.

    Save survival: no new save-path code needed. The unified Patch Engine only touches edited paraIds (I-4);
    resolved imports patch back at their real paraId (pre-existing); the review placeholder carries no paraId
    and is wiped by the same `opLogRef.reset()` every import-mark mount already relies on, so it never reaches
    save. Proven client-side (re-mount from the identical Load-response data reproduces byte-identical
    HTML/marks) in the new `importRoundTrip.test.tsx`; the through-the-wire half is task 054's seam slice.

    Files changed (client only — NO `.cs` files; server-side FR-10 support was already complete, so BFF publish
    size is UNCHANGED by this task): `importedRevisions.ts` (unresolvedItems + renderUnresolvedRevisionPlaceholders),
    `importedRevisions.test.ts` (updated + new coverage), `ComposeEditor.tsx` (wiring at both mount sites),
    `importRoundTrip.test.tsx` (new — FR-10 acceptance suite: render, accept/reject-able incl. deletion-accept
    actually removing text, negative unresolvable-revision-surfaces + unresolvable-comment-parity, save/reload
    determinism). Placement Justification: no new server surface; client-only editor-mount work per the task's
    own `<justification>`.

    Verification: `npx jest importedRevisions importedComments importRoundTrip opaqueAtomTheme` — 4 suites, 30
    tests green. `npm run typecheck` A/B-verified via `git stash` against baseline — byte-identical pre-existing
    error set (8 `@spaarke/ai-widgets`/`@spaarke/document-operations` sibling-dist errors, environmental per root
    CLAUDE.md); zero new errors introduced. Full-mount `ComposeEditor`/`ComposeWorkspace` React-render tests
    could not run in this worktree (pre-existing environmental gap — `@spaarke/ui-components` has no installed
    `node_modules`/built `dist/` here; confirmed via the same `git stash` A/B, already documented by task 024's
    `ComposeEditor.opaqueAtomTheme.test.ts`); `importRoundTrip.test.tsx` exercises the same production code
    paths via `usePendingRedline` (imported `type`-only from `ComposeEditor.tsx`, erased at compile time) over
    a headless editor built from ComposeEditor's own extension set. Full decision record:
    `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/task-053-import-round-trip-decisions.md`.
  </notes>

